From c5b62106987fff2cc9180ac4d344ae02ab9ba1a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:52:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] microblaze: fix latent pattern bugs and
 atomic_test_and_set's result

branch_zero accepted the unsigned comparison codes, and printed them as
the signed branches.  simplify-rtx rewrites unsigned comparisons with
zero first, so this was latent.  Accept only EQ, NE and the signed
codes.

The register-to-register alternatives of movdi and movdf are normally
split after reload, so their templates went unchecked.  movdi printed
a two-operand addk, which does not assemble, and movdf printed a copy
of zero; with the post-reload splits disabled both are reached.  Print
the copies, ordered for overlapping registers as the splits do, and
give movdf's alternative its length of 8.  *one_cmpldi2 printed nor,
which MicroBlaze does not have; the middle end already does not:DI
word by word, so remove it and its split.

atomic_test_and_set returned the old byte, so a byte holding 0x80 gave
128 rather than true.  Return 1 if the byte was not zero and 0
otherwise, as TARGET_ATOMIC_TEST_AND_SET_TRUEVAL, 1, says.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/microblaze/predicates.md (branch_zero_operator): New
	predicate.
	* config/microblaze/microblaze.md (branch_zero): Use it.
	(*one_cmpldi2): Remove, and its split.
	(*movdi_internal): Print a register copy with three-operand addk,
	in an order safe for overlapping registers.
	(*movdf_internal): Likewise rather than a copy of zero, and give
	that alternative a length of 8.
	* config/microblaze/sync.md (atomic_test_and_set): Return whether
	the byte was nonzero.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/microblaze/others/atomic-test-and-set-run.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/others/move-nosplit-run.c: New test.
